WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.450
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.100
SPEAKER 1: If you're
running online retail,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.267
your business depends on
more than just the products

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.130
you offer.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.960
You also need to know
how they're selling

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.780
and how you compare
to your competition.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.480
With Google Market Insights, we
can help you make the most out

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.340
of your data and get
insights that you

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.590
can use to fuel your growth.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.300
Getting started
with Market Insights

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.130
is easy and only
takes two steps.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.880
First, enable Market Insights
through Merchant Center.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.540
And second, set up the
BigQuery Data Transfer Service.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.150
This won't change how you're
using Merchant Center to list

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.980
and manage your product data.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.650
You'll now have access to new
data specifically provided

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.300
to help you see
a bigger picture,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.700
such as seeing how your
prices compare with others

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.100
and being able to discover
the top-selling products

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.540
and brands.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.880
Let's see what insights can
help you grow your business

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.610
by better understanding how
your products are performing,

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.490
how they're priced, and which
products you should consider

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.260
adding to your assortment.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.840
We'll start by looking at the
overview of your products.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.910
To understand how your
products are doing,

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.670
you need a top-line view
of your entire feed.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.810
Drilling down into your
offers by brand and category

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:04.709
lets you check in
on what's popular

00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:07.177
and what may need
your attention.

00:01:07.177 --> 00:01:08.760
In addition, it's
important to keep up

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.160
to date with any
technical or policy issues

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.410
that prevent items
from being listed.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.900
Once you have a better sense
of the health of your feed,

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.447
you can better understand
how to price products.

00:01:18.447 --> 00:01:20.655
There's a lot to factor in
for pricing, including how

00:01:20.655 --> 00:01:22.800
your prices compare to others.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.480
Price benchmarks
help you quickly

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.270
see where your prices sit
against your competition

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.708
and suggest actions
you can take.

00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:32.250
Consider letting your customers
know about your competitively

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.800
priced offerings
and think about ways

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.860
to adjust your pricing for
products above the benchmark.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.290
But what about the products
you're not carrying?

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.790
With the best
sellers report, you

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.440
can keep an eye on
the market and make

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.260
sure you're not missing out
on any popular new items,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.610
like which brands are
selling more than others.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.370
This data can also
be used to figure out

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.830
what categories you can
carry more products in

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.020
and what products you
can carry substitutes

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.508
for when there's high demand.

00:01:56.508 --> 00:01:58.800
Stay informed in areas where
you can grow your business

00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.797
and take action.

00:01:59.797 --> 00:02:01.380
Then measure how
you're performing all

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.387
from a dashboard built from
the Market Insights data.

00:02:04.387 --> 00:02:05.970
These insights can
help you understand

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.040
the best way to grow.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.350
But your business may also have
additional first-party data.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.180
Once you've set up
the export, the data

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.430
is directly accessible
in BigQuery.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.610
From here, you can share the
data directly, build dashboards

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.730
with Data Studio, or
integrate with other tools.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.160
For example, take your
Merchant Center data,

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.650
automate weekly reports in
business intelligence tools

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.650
like Looker and Tableau,
and build a data pipeline

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.080
that combines your selling
information with your supply

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.220
chain data.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.650
Combine these out-of-the-box
insights with your own data

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.818
insights to maximize the
potential for your business.

00:02:37.818 --> 00:02:40.110
If you want to get started,
head to the Merchant Center

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.820
to enable Market Insights.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.820
Then set up exporting
this data to BigQuery.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.980
Check out the link
onscreen to get set up.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.540
Start using insights to
fuel your growth today.

